<title>NORWAY: PGS in seismic deal with Woodside.</title>
<headline>PGS in seismic deal with Woodside.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian offshore services and seismic company Petroleum Geo-Services ASA (PGS) said on Monday it had been selected by Australia's Woodside Offshore Petroleum to perform a three-dimensional (3-D) seismic survey offshore Western Australia.</p>
<p>PGS said it would use the Ramform Challenger vessel to carry out the survey. No value was given for the deal.</p>
<p>The project will be performed in combination with multi-client non-exclusive 3-D work to be sponsored by Woodside and several other major operators in Australia.</p>
<p>The work totals 7,000 square kilometres of 3-D data acquisition and processing and is scheduled to begin in fourth quarter 1997.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
